    <string name="source_dialog_title">Where do the numbers come from?</string>
    <string name="source_dialog_text" formatted="false">AirPods broadcast their battery over Bluetooth to every device nearby. The public part of this broadcast has 10% steps (80%, 90%…). The value shown is what the AirPods send, not a guess.\n\nThe exact percentage (e.g. 87%) comes two ways:\n• If the phone allows it, PodPil connects to the AirPods directly (Apple\'s accessory channel). This works on recent Android builds (e.g. Pixel, Android 16+); on many phones a bug in Android\'s Bluetooth stack still blocks it.\n• Once connected, the AirPods hand over their keys; then the encrypted part of the broadcast gives exact values too. The keys can also be taken from a Mac and entered by hand.</string>
